-- The three live tiers (`ideas`, `active`, `manuscripts`) are flat: one folder per project, directly under the tier. Archive and coauthor are nested: the folder holding a `project.yml` or a `.oculus/project.yml` is the project, and the folders between it and the tier are free filing (`archive/published/<year>/`, `archive/nogo/`, `coauthor/published/<year>/`, `coauthor/active/`, `coauthor/abandoned/`). An id is unique across the whole of `projects/`.
+- The three live tiers (`ideas`, `active`, `manuscripts`) are flat: one folder per project, directly under the tier. Archive and coauthor are nested: the folder holding a `project.yml` or a `.oculus/project.yml` is the project, and the folders between it and the tier are free filing (`archive/published/<year>/`, `archive/failed/`, `archive/stopped/`, `coauthor/published/<year>/`, `coauthor/active/`, `coauthor/stopped/`). An id is unique across the whole of `projects/`.
 - `code/` is the deposit root: its generated `results/` and `figures/` are tracked in the hub and listed in `code/.depositignore`, so the public deposit leaves them out; `code/attic/` holds runnable, documented dead-end experiments that back no published claim. The deposit is tracked in the manifest as `code_availability: { status: none|review-anon|deposited, url, doi }`, and `submit-ready` requires `deposited`.
 - A project's `README.md` `## Data` section records each external dataset (source, version, access, local path, HPC path, cache recipe), and the manifest's `datasets:` lists their registry keys.
-- A project normally moves `idea` -> `active` -> `manuscript` -> published (folder to `archive/published/`) or a dead end (nogo, dropped, disproved, abandoned; folder to `archive/`). A move is a folder move plus setting `type:` and clearing the in-flight status chips.
+- A project normally moves `idea` -> `active` -> `manuscript` -> published (folder to `archive/published/`) or a dead end (failed or stopped; folder to `archive/failed/` or `archive/stopped/`). A move is a folder move plus setting `stage:` and clearing the in-flight status chips.
 
