 title: MS Lipid Handshake (BTD)
 eli5: "Tested whether multiple-sclerosis lesions show a 'lipid handshake': myeloid cells exporting cholesterol from cleared myelin debris coupling, within a lesion, to oligodendrocytes rebuilding myelin. The test scored curated lipid-gene programs and applied block-term and coupled tensor factorization to single-nucleus RNA data across lesion stages."
 outcome: "Disproved. On the powered Macnair 2024 cohort (632k nuclei, 156 samples, 65 paired donor-by-stage), the within-sample myeloid-export to oligo-rebuild coupling is slope -0.06, p=0.73, bootstrap CI [-0.75, 0.14] under donor and stage control; the only significant raw signal is negative (opposite the hypothesis) and a stage confound. Underpowering is excluded at this N. The tensor method machinery is sound (code/ is kept runnable), the biological claim is not. Do not re-attempt the transcriptomic handshake."
